From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:58:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Probe the audio device with a legal sample rate

The probe only wants to know whether a device exists, but FNA checks the rate
before touching the device, so a zero threw ArgumentOutOfRangeException instead
of the NoAudioHardwareException it looks for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
---
 src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/Managers/AudioManager.cs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/Managers/AudioManager.cs b/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/Managers/AudioManager.cs
index 83a148c00..94ce0be14 100644
--- a/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/Managers/AudioManager.cs
+++ b/src/ClassicUO.Client/Game/Managers/AudioManager.cs
@@ -26,7 +26,11 @@ namespace ClassicUO.Game.Managers
         {
             try
             {
-                new DynamicSoundEffectInstance(0, AudioChannels.Stereo).Dispose();
+                // Only here to find out whether an audio device exists at all. The
+                // sample rate has to be a legal one: FNA validates it before it ever
+                // touches the device, so a zero throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException
+                // instead of the NoAudioHardwareException this is looking for.
+                new DynamicSoundEffectInstance(44100, AudioChannels.Stereo).Dispose();
             }
             catch (NoAudioHardwareException ex)
             {
